.TH sane\-ix1300 5 "10 Oct 2026" "@PACKAGEVERSION@" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.IX sane\-ix1300
.SH NAME
sane\-ix1300 \- SANE backend for the ScanSnap iX1300 on a Wi\-Fi network
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sane\-ix1300
library implements a SANE (Scanner Access Now Easy) backend. The backend
controls a PFU (Fujitsu) ScanSnap iX1300 scanner through the Wi\-Fi
network. It uses TCP and UDP. It does not use USB.
.PP
For USB, use the
.BR sane\-fujitsu (5)
backend.
.PP
The backend sends the same network commands as the PFU software.
The scanner sends a JPEG image for each side of a sheet.
The backend decodes the JPEG data to raw lines.

.SH DEVICE NAMES
The device name is the IPv4 address of the scanner, for example:
.PP
.RS
ix1300:192.0.2.212
.RE

.SH HOST ID
The scanner keeps one registered host ID (8 bytes). The scanner accepts
commands only from a host that sends this ID. ScanSnap Home registers a
random ID for each computer.
.PP
Write the registered ID in the configuration file with the
.B hostid
line. If the ID is not correct, the scanner refuses the reserve with the
result \-6. Then
.B sane_open
gives SANE_STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, and the debug output shows the ID.
.PP
If ScanSnap Home on a different computer connects to the scanner, it
registers its own ID. Then you must register your ID again.

.SH RESERVE AND KEEPALIVE
.B sane_open
sends a reserve to the scanner.
.B sane_close
sends a release. While the device is open, a thread sends a keepalive
packet at intervals. If the backend stops without a release, the scanner
frees the reserve after the reserve timeout plus 10 seconds.
.PP
If a different host has the reserve,
.B sane_open
gives SANE_STATUS_DEVICE_BUSY.
.PP
If the scanner does not answer a keepalive, or if it sends a power or
release event, the next
.B sane_start
sends a keepalive again. If there is no reply, the backend searches the
scanner again and makes a new reserve. This is necessary after the
scanner turns itself off and you turn it on again.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-source "ADF Front" | "ADF Back" | "ADF Duplex"
Selects the side of the sheet. The backend uses the names of the scanner.
Window 0 is the front.
.PP
.RS
CAUTION: Usually you load the paper with the printed side down. Then the
print is on the
.B back
side. For a single\-sided document, use
.BR "\-\-source \(dqADF Back\(dq" .
.PP
With "ADF Duplex", the backend gives two frames for each sheet: first the
front, then the back.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-mode Color | Gray | Lineart
Selects the scan mode. Lineart is a software threshold of the gray image.
.TP
.B \-\-resolution 150 | 200 | 300 | 600
Selects the resolution in dpi.
.TP
.B \-\-page\-width, \-\-page\-height
Set the size of the paper in mm. The maximum width is 219.4 mm.
The maximum height is 895.5 mm. With the maximum height, the scanner
uses its automatic length.
.TP
.B \-l, \-t, \-x, \-y
Set the scan area in the page. The backend cuts this area from the
image in software.
.TP
.B \-\-threshold 0..255
In Lineart mode, a pixel with a gray value less than this value is black.
.TP
.B \-\-ald yes | no
Automatic length detection. The default is yes. The scanner finds the end
of the paper, and the backend removes the empty area after the paper.
Before
.BR sane_start ,
the backend does not know the height. Then the parameters show
lines = \-1. After
.BR sane_start ,
the height is correct.
.TP
.B \-\-compression None | JPEG
None (the default) gives raw lines. JPEG gives the JPEG data of the
scanner in a frame of type SANE_FRAME_JPEG (11). SANE 1.0 does not have
this frame type, and most frontends cannot use it.
.TP
.B \-\-halt\-on\-cancel yes | no
Selects what a cancel does with the paper (see
.BR "PAPER FEED AND CANCEL" ).
With no (the default), the scanner feeds out the rest of the stack
without a scan. With yes, the paper stops in the paper path, and you must
open the ADF top section and remove it. This option has the name and the
text of the same option of the
.B fujitsu
backend.
.TP
.B \-\-scan, \-\-long\-press, \-\-page\-loaded
Sensors (read only). The value of
.B scan
is yes one time after a short press of the scan button.
The value of
.B long\-press
is yes one time after a long press (about 3 seconds).
The value of
.B page\-loaded
is yes when there is paper in the paper chute.
The backend reads the button from the GET HW STATUS command and from the
trigger packets that the scanner sends to the host. A frontend such as
.BR scanbd (8)
can read these options.

.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration file is
.IR @CONFIGDIR@/ix1300.conf .
Lines that start with "#" are comments. These lines are possible:
.TP
.B net auto
Find scanners with a UDP broadcast to port 52217.
.TP
.B net <ip>
Find the scanner at this address. You can write more than one line.
.TP
.B hostid <16 hex digits>
The registered host ID. If you do not set it, the backend uses the MAC
address and two zero bytes.
.TP
.B iface <name>
The network interface. If you do not set it, the backend uses the route to
the scanner.
.TP
.B timeout <seconds>
The longest time for one complete reply. The default is 30.
.TP
.B reserve\-timeout <seconds>
The scanner frees the reserve when it gets no keepalive packet for this
time plus 10 seconds. The default is 30.
.TP
.B keepalive <seconds>
The time between two keepalive packets. The default is 15. The backend
makes the value smaller if it is too long for the reserve timeout.
.TP
.B discovery\-timeout <milliseconds>
The time that the backend waits for discovery replies. The default is 3000.
.TP
.B trigger\-port <port>
The UDP port for the scan button packets. The default 0 lets the system
select a port.

.SH STATUS VALUES
.TP
.B SANE_STATUS_NO_DOCS
The chute is empty: END OF PAPER (sense 3/80/03) for E0 or for the first
READ of a new sheet, before image data.
.TP
.B SANE_STATUS_JAMMED
A paper jam, a double feed, or a lost sheet (sense 3/80/03 on the back
side or after image data).
.TP
.B SANE_STATUS_IO_ERROR
No new image data for 60 seconds, a side that is not complete in 600
seconds, a side larger than 64 MiB, a bad reply, or JPEG data that is not
complete or not valid. The backend does not add lines that are not in
the JPEG data.
.TP
.B SANE_STATUS_DEVICE_BUSY
An option change during a job. Call
.B sane_cancel
first.
.PP
.B sane_cancel
can come from a signal handler or a different thread. If
.B sane_start
or
.B sane_read
runs at that time, the call stops at its next safe point and gives
SANE_STATUS_CANCELLED.

.SH "PAPER FEED AND CANCEL"
The scanner feeds all sheets in the chute in one job. It does not wait
for the host, and there is no clean stop after a number of sheets.
.B Load only the sheets that you want to scan.
.PP
The frontend sets the page limit, for example
.BR "scanimage \-\-batch\-count=N" .
With "ADF Duplex", each sheet gives two pages. At the end of the stack,
E0 gives END OF PAPER (sense 3/80/03), and the backend sends END JOB
(D6) only.
.PP
When the frontend stops before the end of the stack, it calls
.BR sane_cancel .
.B sane_cancel
(and
.B sane_close
in a job) sends CANCEL READ (D8), then E0. On the iX1300, E0 after D8
makes the scanner feed out
.B the rest of the stack without a scan.
The backend waits until GET HW STATUS (C2) shows an empty chute and a
clear paper path (at most 120 seconds), then sends D6. After D8, a READ
gives sense 5/24/00, so the backend sends no READ.
.PP
With
.BR "\-\-halt\-on\-cancel=yes" ,
.B sane_cancel
sends D8 and D6 only. The motor stops at once, and D6 does not eject
paper. A sheet that the scanner already pulled in can stop in the paper
path, or it can still come out; this depends on how far it was. The rest
of the stack stays in the chute. If paper stays in the path, open the ADF
top section and remove it before the next scan.
.PP
After an error (for example a paper jam or a timeout), the backend sends
D8 and D6 only. Remove the paper by hand.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/ix1300.conf
The backend configuration file.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-ix1300.so
The shared library of the backend.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SANE_CONFIG_DIR
This environment variable specifies the list of directories that can
contain the configuration file.
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_IX1300
If the library was compiled with debug support enabled, this environment
variable controls the debug level for this backend. Higher values give
more output. 1 shows errors, 5 shows the important events and the sense
data, 15 shows each network command, and 30 shows hex dumps.

.SH LIMITS
.IP \(bu 2
The backend has no TLS. A scanner in the "RED" or "SEC" mode uses TLS
ports. The backend cannot use such a scanner.
.IP \(bu 2
The backend does not register a host ID. Register the ID over USB first.
.IP \(bu 2
The paper must be in the top paper chute (ADF). The front slot (return
path) is not available.
.IP \(bu 2
The maximum page height is 895.5 mm. Long paper mode is not available.
.IP \(bu 2
The scanner selects the color automatically. If the scanner sends a gray
image in Color mode, the backend converts it to RGB.
.IP \(bu 2
A paper jam on Wi\-Fi does not always give an error. The page then ends at
the jam point.
.IP \(bu 2
There is no clean stop after N sheets. A cancel feeds out the rest of the
stack without a scan, or (with
.BR \-\-halt\-on\-cancel )
leaves the paper in the paper path.
.IP \(bu 2
The backend accepts discovery replies and trigger packets only from the
address of the scanner. This is a filter on the LAN, not an
authentication.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sane (7),
.BR sane\-fujitsu (5),
.BR scanimage (1),
.BR scanbd (8)

.SH AUTHOR
The ix1300 backend authors.
